\subsection{Hardware-Agnostic Determinism}

All simulations are executed under strict deterministic posture:

\begin{itemize}
    \item IEEE 754 floating-point compliance,
    \item deterministic PRNG seeding,
    \item reproducible multi-threading (Rayon),
    \item reproducible GPU compute shaders (OpenCL/CUDA),
    \item strict memory-safety guarantees.
\end{itemize}

Let $\mathcal{H}$ denote the set of hardware substrates. Determinism requires:

\[
\forall h_i, h_j \in \mathcal{H},\quad
\mathrm{Sim}(h_i) = \mathrm{Sim}(h_j).
\]

